  "decisions": [
    "Farmyard Commando is the first production adoption target; existing Tinderbox conformance and shared asset exchange remain valid.",
    "A la carte adoption permits asset-only, individual-system and composed-runtime paths with host-supplied providers.",
    "Platform input/presentation, game rules and device quality are separate profiles.",
    "Current public schemas, headless cores, resource preservation and explicit unsupported rejection remain required.",
    "PC sprite and 3D battle control implementations differ; historical design and chronological rule values are not assumed current.",
    "Farmyard README mission/fire limitations lag the current pinned runtime; physical-phone performance and native packaging remain unverified.",
    "No new cast, species/class perks, universal game scheduler or automatic consumer migration is introduced."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Git objects were read at complete immutable commits without changing donor worktrees.",
    "Hashes identify reference material; this inventory does not ship donor bytes or grant additional asset rights.",
    "Existing attack/fire/climbing/damage assessments retain the separately recorded source pins in docs/reviews/2026-10-28-design-tradeoffs.md.",
    "The blueprint describes proposed responsibilities and acceptance evidence, not implemented public module exports."
  ]
